SurfaceFlinger: keep the layer LUT descriptor open in screenshots

Project: frameworks/native (TrebleDroid android-16.0 fork of AOSP android-16.0.0_r2)

When a screenshot contains an HDR layer, ScreenCaptureOutput asks the display HAL for the
tone-mapping LUT of that layer (IComposerClient.getLuts) and hands it to the renderer. In
android-16.0.0_r2 the descriptor is taken from a temporary:

    base::unique_fd(aidlLuts.pfd.dup().get())

dup() returns a ScopedFileDescriptor that owns the new descriptor, get() only reads its number,
and unique_fd then claims the same number. At the end of the statement the temporary closes
it. fdsan aborts the process there, and the render thread fails to map what is left:

    Abort message: attempted to close file descriptor 737, expected to be unowned,
                   actually owned by unique_fd 0x745d470790
      ndk::internal::closeWithError
      android::ScreenCaptureOutput::generateClientCompositionRequests
      ...
      android::SurfaceFlinger::captureDisplay
    Abort message: mmap failed
      android::renderengine::skia::LutShader::lutShader

Seen on the device on 2026-10-10 (third DSU session): a screenshot of the Motorola Camera
viewfinder in video mode, which is an HDR layer, killed surfaceflinger and with it the whole
framework. The display HAL of this phone implements getLuts; a HAL that returns nothing never
reaches the line. Task snapshots and the rotation animation use the same code.

Upstream has the fix: android-16.0.0_r3, android-16.0.0_r4 and android16-qpr2-release read

    base::unique_fd(aidlLuts.pfd.release())

This patch changes the one expression to exactly that. It can be dropped when the tree moves
to android-16.0.0_r3 or later.

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/ScreenCaptureOutput.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/ScreenCaptureOutput.cpp
index 2906bbd..22c3e48 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/ScreenCaptureOutput.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/ScreenCaptureOutput.cpp
@@ -183,7 +183,7 @@ ScreenCaptureOutput::generateClientCompositionRequests(
                             static_cast<int32_t>(aidlLuts.lutProperties[j].samplingKeys[0]));
                 }
                 layer.luts = std::make_shared<gui::DisplayLuts>(base::unique_fd(
-                                                                        aidlLuts.pfd.dup().get()),
+                                                                        aidlLuts.pfd.release()),
                                                                 offsets, dimensions, sizes, keys);
             }
         }
